wing to \u00b12000/\u00b11000 (steps 16\u201317) keeps the boundary crisp.\n\n4. **Volume is not the driver (confounder).** Group event counts are flat-to-dipping across the period (113/137/118/133/66/71/120/119/150/104, step 02); the bin containing the change point is a *low* bin. So this is a change of *whom*, not *how much*.\n\n5. **Popularity/hub is not the driver (confounder).** No group member is a hub except 1374 (rank 10, step 28), and members have uniform ~93\u201397 events / ~31\u201336 partners (step 03) \u2014 the switch is not an artifact of high-degree nodes.\n\n6. **Background turnover control.** Hubs 733 and 1566 also churn partners across 40166 (steps 29\u201332, Jaccard \u22480.07 and \u22480.05), so churn per se is ambient in this graph. What distinguishes the group is *synchrony and shared cohort identity*: the hubs' pre/post sets are idiosyncratic and non-overlapping with each other, whereas the 12 group members trade the *same* old set for the *same* new set at the *same* instant. Steps 26\u201327 confirm the cohorts are temporally disjoint (old partners ~0 events after, new partners ~0 events before), consistent with a genuine regime boundary rather than reshuffling within a stable pool.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_cd75e8ee\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [103, 462, 719, 836, 866, 1224, 1318, 1374, 1415, 1598, 1610, 1826],\n  \"window\": [35166, 45166],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"narrative\": \"The group undergoes an abrupt, coordinated regime switch at t\u224840166. With \u00b15000 half-windows, every member tested (103, 462, 836, 1224, 1415, 1598, 1826) has exactly zero overlap between its pre- and post-contact sets (Jaccard 0.00), and the sets are internally stable: node 103 reuses the same partners across three pre-windows and then a different stable pool across three post-windows, so this is two regimes joined by a sharp boundary rather than gradual drift. The switch is colle